    "why": "The data authority's canonical OHLC is built from the BID series. A long signalled on bid actually enters at ask (bid + spread) and exits at bid, so the entire round-trip spread is incurred once, at entry. A short is the mirror image. Charging a further spread at each exit would bill a two-partial trade for three round trips."
  },
